Apple is testing a standalone <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> chatbot app for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, reports <em><a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-03-24/ios-27-features-apple-ai-reboot-with-siri-app-new-interface-ask-siri-button">Bloomberg</a></em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a>. Apple plans to debut a chatbot version of &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; that will compete with Claude and ChatGPT, and the new &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; could be accessible through a dedicated app.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/08/Finder-Siri-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1014637" /><br/>
Gurman previously said that Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/01/21/siri-chatbot-ios-27/">was not going to develop</a> a standalone &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; app, but it appears plans have changed. It was not clear how the rumored chatbot version of &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; was going to work without an app, because people often have multiple back-and-forth text-based conversations with chatbots, and not having a dedicated space would have been confusing.<br/>
<br/>
Like ChatGPT and Claude, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; will support both text and voice-based conversations. The app will display either a list or grid of past conversations, with options to favorite chats, search through chats, initiate new chats, and save chats. Conversations with &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; will resemble iMessage conversations, with Apple using chat bubbles. New conversations will start with suggested prompts on what to ask.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; will be able to do much of what current chatbots can do, such as searching the web with visually rich results, providing summaries, and evaluating uploaded documents, and the personal assistant will still be integrated into Apple devices. Pressing the side button on an iPhone or using the &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; wake word will activate &zwnj;Siri&zwnj;. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; integration will replace the current Spotlight search functionality, but Apple plans to keep and expand on &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; Suggestions. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; Suggestions will have more access to user data to provide more relevant prompts.<br/>
<br/>
Chatbot &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; will have an updated look to go along with the dedicated app. Activating &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; will have a new animation that prompts the user to search or ask a question, and Gurman says Apple is testing a version of &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; integrated into the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>. Apple's test interface includes a glowing &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; icon and a "searching" label in the &zwnj;Dynamic Island&zwnj; while &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; is processing a request, and once done, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; expands into a larger translucent panel with the results. Pulling down on the menu initiates an interface for a conversation.<br/>
<br/>
It's also possible Apple will integrate an "Ask &zwnj;Siri&zwnj;" button into the menus of other apps, giving users a way to send content directly to &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; alongside a request. The iOS keyboard could get a Write with &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; option that surfaces Writing Tools.<br/>
<br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; features that were originally planned for iOS 18 will be introduced in &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;, with &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; able to use personal data and context to answer queries. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; will also be able to do more in and between apps, and will be able to see what's on the user's screen. Apple promised that those features would appear before the end of 2026.<br/>
<br/>
